- Ensure runtime compilation choices do not alter state-dict key compatibility; either construct the VAE exactly as training did or make the compile choice explicit and verify strict loading against the completed checkpoint.
- Keep the evaluator's strict checkpoint load and fail with a concise diagnostic identifying config/checkpoint mismatches.
- Add tests for: stored-hparams reconstruction, baseline fallback, strict DreamSim checkpoint load, checkpoint selection, and preservation of the test metric configuration.
- Run the corrected evaluator on the epoch-89 checkpoint with batch size 1; verify both `test_step` loss logging and post-hoc reconstruction metrics complete.
- Only after successful evaluation, update the run log/README/report with the measured CSV results and corrected invocation.

